Package: ThermalScapeR
Title: Landscape-Scale Microclimate and Endotherm Energetics Modeling
    Tools
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: person("Bryan", "Spencer", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                   email = "bspencer@uidaho.edu")
Description: A collection of tools for downloading, preprocessing, and
    packaging spatial and remote-sensing data from Google Earth Engine
    and NOAA AORC for two linked, landscape-scale modeling pipelines
    built on the NicheMapR ecosystem: fine-scale microclimate modeling
    (via a fork of 'microclimf') and endotherm thermal-energetics
    modeling (via a proprietary, advanced NicheMapR Endotherm model
    executable). Both pipelines support tiled, HPC/SLURM-ready
    workflows for large study areas.
